"""
FOR TESTING
OHT Fleet Controller  —  multiple OHTs on one loop, no collisions
=====================================================================
Run in Omniverse / Isaac Sim:  Window > Script Editor > paste > Run (Ctrl+Enter),
they start moving right away.  Re-running the script rebuilds the fleet cleanly.
To stop it:  run   import builtins; builtins._oht_fleet.stop()

What it does
  * Clones /World/OHT2grip_Revised into /World/OHT_Fleet/OHT_01..N
    (the original is hidden and used only as a template).
  * Drives every OHT along one closed rail loop (ROUTE_XY below).
    Corners are true circular arcs (CORNER_RADIUS_M), like the real rail.
    Each OHT rides on a front and a rear bogie, so in curves the body sits
    on the chord between them (BOGIE_HALF_SPACING_M).
  * Each OHT measures the gap to the vehicle ahead along the rail and
    - cruises at V_MAX when the way is clear,
    - slows down smoothly as the gap closes (time-headway + braking curve),
    - stops behind a stopped vehicle, keeping at least MIN_GAP_M.
    A hard position clamp guarantees vehicles can never overlap.
  * Slows down automatically in curves.
  * Adds more ground machines under the rail (NEW_MACHINE_PORTS) and puts
    magazines on half of them. Empty OHTs go to a machine with a magazine:
    stop, lower the hoist, close the claws, lift the magazine and carry it
    to an empty machine, lower, open the claws, raise, leave.
    Followers queue up behind a working OHT.

IMPORTANT: if another script/extension is still moving OHT2grip_Revised
(e.g. your original move-and-grab script), stop it first.
"""

